   "data": {
    "text": "Replay run for **4 Jul 2025 Guadalupe** completed:\n\n**Run `r_cfef067dcc52b9c2`** - `85 mm / 12h + gauged river inflows`, `sim_hours 12`\n> `has_river_inflows = true` - inflows are built into every run.\n\nOverall:\n* `buildings_flooded: 1863`, `severe: 1637`, `own_cell: 1063`\n* `people_exposed: 1067`\n* `road_km_impassable: 114.865 km` at 0.3m threshold\n* `flooded_area_km2: 11.9377`, `max_depth_m: 13.109`\n* `peak_t_s: 23400` = 6.5h after storm start\n* `rain_volume_m3: 26892507.6` vs `inflow_volume_m3: 163278626.1` - inflow dominates ~6x rain. Planning model, not a forecast.\n\n### South Fork - camps and corridors\n\nAll South Fork places flood severely:\n\n**South Fork Guadalupe River corridor:**\n* `buildings_flooded: 134`, `own_cell: 129`, `people: 60`\n* `road_km_impassable: 21.275`, `flooded_area_km2: 1.2431`\n* `max_depth_m: 12.188`\n\n**Camp Mystic Guadalupe River - centroid [-99.37143,30.0092]:**\n* `buildings_flooded: 33`, `own_cell: 30`, `people: 10`\n* `road_km_impassable: 2.765`, `flooded_area_km2: 0.1283`\n* `max_depth_m: 13.109` - deepest point in study area\n\n**Camp Mystic Cypress Lake:**\n* `buildings_flooded: 17`, `own_cell: 11`, `people: 0`\n* `road_km_impassable: 0.977`, `flooded_area_km2: 0.0559`\n* `max_depth_m: 5.531`\n\n**Heart O' the Hills Summer Camp for Girls:**\n* `buildings_flooded: 12`, `own_cell: 8`, `people: 6`\n* `road_km_impassable: 1.566`, `flooded_area_km2: 0.0395`\n* `max_depth_m: 9.445`\n\nOther camps in AOI:\n\n**Camp La Junta for Boys:**\n* `33? No: 30 flooded, 13 own_cell, 13 people, 2.749 km road, max 10.445 m, 0.1644 km2`\n\n**Camp Waldemar:**\n* `26 flooded, 7 own_cell, 8 people, 5.475 km road, max 6.941 m, 0.2466 km2`\n\nContext corridors / towns in same run:\n* **Guadalupe River:** `300 flooded, 211 own_cell, 229 people, 31.303 km road, max 10.625 m, 2.7098 km2`\n* **North Fork Guadalupe River:** `43 flooded, 31 own_cell, 15 people, 11.11 km road, max 6.941 m, 1.299 km2`\n* **Hunt:** `187 flooded, 109 own_cell, 103 people, 13.244 km road, max 10.445 m, 1.4766 km2`\n* **Ingram:** `265 flooded, 152 own_cell, 164 people, 9.691 km road, max 7.988 m, 0.957 km2`\n\n> `buildings_flooded` = footprint touches flood, `own_cell` = building cell itself wet.\n\n### Shelters reachable?\n\nTested at peak `t_s=23400` in same run `r_cfef067dcc52b9c2`:\n\nFrom South Fork camps - **NOT reachable to any shelter at peak:**\n* `rt_bc78617d1dd8` - Camp Mystic Guadalupe River -> `reachable:false`, `edges_removed:874`\n* `rt_fa0f3f9ff42a` - Heart O' the Hills -> `reachable:false`\n* `rt_3d22dfb68005` - Camp La Junta -> `reachable:false`\n* `rt_afdd6dfe632b` - Camp Waldemar -> `reachable:false`\n\nEarly window from Mystic existed, then closed:\n* `rt_b838d7627481` - `t_s=0`, Mystic -> **The Hunt School (candidate shelter (assumed))** `reachable:true, 9.245 km, 138.7 min`\n* `rt_d6d0c6374635` - `t_s=7200` (2h), same path still `reachable:true, 9.245 km, 138.7 min, edges_removed:60`\n* By `t_s=23400` same origin unreachable.\n\nTown centres retain very local access at peak:\n* `rt_5464f54c177f` - Hunt centroid -> **The Hunt School** `reachable:true, 0.319 km, 4.8 min`\n* `rt_891eadf119e0` - Ingram centroid -> **Ingram Elementary School** `reachable:true, 0.889 km, 13.3 min`\n\nInterpretation: in this replay all named camps along the South Fork and both Forks/main stem flood with multi-metre maxima and km of impassable road. At peak flow the South Fork camps are isolated from the shelter network, while Hunt and Ingram retain short routes to their nearest assumed shelters. Early evacuation before peak was the only modelled window from Camp Mystic to Hunt School.\n"
   }
